---
// The shared face pipeline: sample, detect, cache, then each model's crop.
import { FG } from "../../lib/figures";
---

<figure class="fig">
            <div style="border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--card); padding: 20px; display: grid; gap: 16px; min-width: 0">
              <div style="font: 500 11.5px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--muted)">Video and images · one shared face detector, then each model's own crop</div>
              <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: var(--f-dir); gap: 10px; align-items: stretch">
                <div style="flex: var(--f-item); border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--paper); padding: 12px; display: grid; gap: 8px; align-content: start; min-width: 0; font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.4">
                  <span style="font: 500 11.5px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--accent-ink)">1 · sample</span>
                  <strong style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem">32 frames, evenly spaced</strong>
                  <div aria-hidden="true" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(8, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 3px; height: 30px; max-width: 220px">{FG.frames.map((x) => (<Fragment><span style="position: relative; background: var(--tint); border: 1px solid var(--rule-2)"><span style={`position: absolute; left: ${x.l}; top: 20%; width: 32%; height: 52%; border: 1px solid var(--stone); border-radius: 50%`}></span></span></Fragment>))}</div>
                  <span style="color: var(--muted)">An image is a one-frame clip.</span>
                </div>
                <span aria-hidden="true" style="flex: none; align-self: center; font: 500 15px/1 var(--mono); color: var(--muted)"><i class="arr"></i></span>
                <div style="flex: var(--f-item); border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--paper); padding: 12px; display: grid; gap: 8px; align-content: start; min-width: 0; font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.4">
                  <span style="font: 500 11.5px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--accent-ink)">2 · detect</span>
                  <strong style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem">SCRFD-10GF, on CPU</strong>
                  <div aria-hidden="true" style="position: relative; height: 72px; max-width: 220px; background: var(--tint); border: 1px solid var(--rule-2)">
                    <span style="position: absolute; left: 12%; top: 34%; width: 13%; height: 34%; border: 1px dashed var(--stone)"></span>
                    <span style="position: absolute; left: 48%; top: 12%; width: 30%; height: 76%; border: 1.5px solid var(--ink)"></span>
                    <span style="position: absolute; left: 57%; top: 38%; width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); transform: translate(-50%, -50%)"></span>
                    <span style="position: absolute; left: 69%; top: 38%; width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); transform: translate(-50%, -50%)"></span>
                    <span style="position: absolute; left: 63%; top: 53%; width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); transform: translate(-50%, -50%)"></span>
                    <span style="position: absolute; left: 58%; top: 68%; width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); transform: translate(-50%, -50%)"></span>
                    <span style="position: absolute; left: 68%; top: 68%; width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); transform: translate(-50%, -50%)"></span>
                  </div>
                  <span style="color: var(--muted)">Keeps the largest face per frame: its box and five landmarks.</span>
                </div>
                <span aria-hidden="true" style="flex: none; align-self: center; font: 500 15px/1 var(--mono); color: var(--muted)"><i class="arr"></i></span>
                <div style="flex: var(--f-item); border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--paper); padding: 12px; display: grid; gap: 8px; align-content: start; min-width: 0; font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.4">
                  <span style="font: 500 11.5px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--accent-ink)">3 · cache</span>
                  <strong style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem">Detections, saved once</strong>
                  <code style="font: 400 11.5px/1.45 var(--mono); color: var(--ink-2); overflow-wrap: anywhere">faces/&lt;dataset&gt;/&lt;detector&gt;__&lt;hash&gt;/</code>
                  <span style="color: var(--muted)">Every model reuses them; a changed setting gets a new folder.</span>
                </div>
                <span aria-hidden="true" style="flex: none; align-self: center; font: 500 15px/1 var(--mono); color: var(--muted)"><i class="arr"></i></span>
                <div style="flex: var(--f-item); border: 1px solid var(--ink); background: var(--paper); padding: 12px; display: grid; gap: 8px; align-content: start; min-width: 0; font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.4">
                  <span style="font: 500 11.5px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--accent-ink)">4 · crop and score</span>
                  <strong style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem">Each model cuts its own crop</strong>
                  <div style="display: grid; gap: 5px">
                    <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2px 8px; align-items: baseline"><code style="font: 500 11.5px/1 var(--mono); padding: 4px 6px; background: var(--tint)">five_point</code><span>aligned on the landmarks</span></div>
                    <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2px 8px; align-items: baseline"><code style="font: 500 11.5px/1 var(--mono); padding: 4px 6px; background: var(--tint)">none</code><span>a square around the box</span></div>
                    <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2px 8px; align-items: baseline"><code style="font: 500 11.5px/1 var(--mono); padding: 4px 6px; background: var(--tint)">box</code><span>the box, widened and stretched</span></div>
                  </div>
                  <span style="color: var(--muted)">Clip score: the mean of frame scores.</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 10px; align-items: baseline; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 1px dashed var(--rule-2); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.45"><code style="font: 500 12px/1 var(--mono); padding: 4px 6px; background: var(--bad); color: var(--paper)">no_face</code><span style="flex: 1 1 280px; min-width: 0">Fewer than 8 frames with a face (video) or none (image). Counted per group, never dropped: face detectors fail more often on darker skin.</span></div>
            </div>
            <figcaption><strong>The face pipeline.</strong> Tight face crops get one retry with a black border. Frame-run models (HAVIC, LipForensics) sample their own frames and get their own cache.</figcaption>
          </figure>
